<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"  xml:id="chapter-11-intro">
  <title>Week 11</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      At the end of this week you should be able to...
    </p>
    <objectives>
      <ul>
        <li>trace the flow of control during the execution of a program using for loops</li>
        <li>use a debugger to trace through call stacks and nested loops</li>
        <li>apply pair-programming to method development</li>
        <li>recognize common patterns in the development of methods working over collections of data such as strings and arrays</li>
      </ul>
    </objectives>
  </introduction>
  <xi:include href="sec-method-development-patterns.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="sec-nested-loops.ptx"/>
</chapter>
